# Local debug session

When the human says run the app locally, start the server, attach a browser
debug session, and keep watching. Do not hand off a URL.

- Pages UI without a backend: `npm run dev:web` -w @opensesame/pages on
  `http://localhost:5180` (localhost, not 127.0.0.1, for passkeys).
- Full stack: `npm run dev`. -w @opensesame/pages
- Keep the Vite process attached. Open the origin. Watch console, pageerror,
  and failed requests with full stacks.
- Patch source so HMR updates the same session. Do not kill it to run
  `dist/` or a headless `verify:*` gate unless that gate was requested.
- Stop the session only when the human says stop.

Procedure: `skills/local-debug-session/SKILL.md`. Canonical rule: `AGENTS.md` §5.
